 ### Intelligence levels
 
 For `normal` chats: `instant` → `medium` → `high` → `extra_high` → `pro`.
-Higher levels use more capable models and deeper thinking. `pro` uses
-`gpt-5-5-pro`. You can also pin a specific `model` and `thinking_effort`
-(`min` / `standard` / `extended` / `max`).
+The default is `extra_high`, which resolves to `gpt-5-6-thinking` at `max`
+thinking — the newest non-pro thinker that is confirmed to serve its own model.
+`pro` uses `gpt-6-pro`. You can also pin a specific `model` and
+`thinking_effort` (`min` / `standard` / `extended` / `max`).
+
+> No intelligence tier maps to a `*-wm` "work model". `gpt-6-astra-wm` silently
+> serves `gpt-5-mini` at every effort while echoing the requested slug in
+> `default_model_slug`, so it is never used. When you pin a `model` explicitly,
+> the served model is `resolved_model_slug` (then `model_slug`), never
+> `default_model_slug` — see `src/served.ts`.
+
+### `/gpt` command
+
+Command Governor adds a deterministic `/gpt` slash command
+(`extensions/gpt-command.ts`) that drives your ChatGPT account with **zero
+harness-model tokens** — Prime runs the handler as code on the keystroke:
+
+- `/gpt review [gpt|pro|max] [context]` — gathers the working-tree diff (vs the
+  merge-base with the default branch) and sends it to a **brand-new** ChatGPT
+  conversation for review. Fresh context is deliberate: a session reviewing its
+  own work shares the context that made the mistake. `gpt` (default) =
+  `gpt-5-6-thinking@max`, unmetered, for reviewing everything; `pro` =
+  `gpt-6-pro`, a capped lane reserved for hard reviews; `max` = a fresh Claude
+  reviewer via the harness (metered — the command prints the exact path rather
+  than faking an in-process Claude reviewer).
+- `/gpt research <topic>` — cited Pro-tier deep research (the capped lane;
+  surfaces the deep-research rate-limit fields and errors if the quota is spent).
+- `/gpt chat <prompt> [--model <slug>] [--effort <min|standard|extended|max>]` —
+  ad-hoc one-shot in a fresh chat; `--model`/`--effort` tab-complete from the
+  account's real model list.
+
+Every reply's served model is asserted against what was requested. If the
+backend serves a different or downgraded model, `/gpt` errors loudly and never
+retries on a lesser model.
 
